      "id": 161113,
      "name": "Alex",
      "username": "Alex",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/alex/{size}/2059_2.png",
      "created_at": "2016-02-10T06:19:02.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Void is a really unusual thing to associate with powers of nature and harmony, since it evokes emptiness and silence. I'd say maybe it's associated with outer space, but we already have \"cosmic\" for things like that. I remember in&nbsp;<em>Homestuck</em> the void aspect was the one thing that even the omniscient could not see through, allowing characters to keep secrets even from god-tier beings... What if drawing power from the void is a way to tap into the most primal thing imaginable, the most ancient of ancient forces, the thing that existed before even existance did. If so, it would be a sort of Alpha to OblivAeon's Omega, fighting the ultimate end with the ultimate beginning?</p>",
      "post_number": 3,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:41:40.040Z",
